          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 30-year-old woman presents with a 3 cm breast lump. On examination, the lump i</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 30-year-old woman presents with a 3 cm breast lump. On examination, the lump is smooth, firm, and mobile. Which imaging modality should be used first-line in her triple assessment?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mammography</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Mammography is first-line for women over 35–40, when the breast becomes more fatty. In a younger woman with dense breast tissue, mammography has lower sensitivity.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ultrasonography</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. In women under 35, breast tissue is dense, making ultrasound the first-line imaging modality. It reliably distinguishes solid from cystic lesions and is safe in pregnancy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Contrast-enhanced MRI of the breast</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>MRI is reserved for specific indications such as screening BRCA carriers or assessing disease extent in confirmed cancer, not as a first-line investigation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Computed tomography of the chest</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CT is not part of standard breast triple assessment. It is used for staging distant metastases in confirmed malignancy, not for initial evaluation of a breast lump.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "For women under 35, breast tissue is dense, so ultrasound is the first-line imaging modality in triple assessment. Mammography becomes first-line only after age 35–40."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Ultrasound is first-line for women under 35 because their dense breast tissue limits mammographic sensitivity."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
