          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 25-year-old woman has a 2 cm breast lump confirmed as a fibroadenoma on concor</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 25-year-old woman has a 2 cm breast lump confirmed as a fibroadenoma on concordant triple assessment. She is asymptomatic. What is the most appropriate management?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Wide local excision with clear margins</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Wide local excision with clear margins is the recommended approach for phyllodes tumours, which can recur if inadequately excised. A small fibroadenoma does not require this.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Observation with follow-up</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. A small, concordant fibroadenoma can be safely observed. Excision is considered only if the lump exceeds 3–4 cm or shows growth on follow-up.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Incision and drainage with anti-staphylococcal antibiotics</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incision and drainage with antibiotics is the management for a lactational breast abscess caused by Staphylococcus aureus, not for a fibroadenoma.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mastectomy with axillary clearance</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Mastectomy is reserved for large or multifocal breast cancers. It is vastly disproportionate for a confirmed benign fibroadenoma.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "A small, concordant fibroadenoma is managed by observation. Excision is indicated only when the lesion exceeds 3–4 cm or is actively growing."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! A small fibroadenoma confirmed by concordant triple assessment can be safely observed, with excision reserved for larger or growing lesions."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
